Multiple economic indicators have declined, indicating a poor start to the year for Taiwan’s economy – China News Service
Xinhua News Agency, Taipei, February 11 (Reporters Zhao Bo, Huang Yang) The volume of export trade has declined for five consecutive months; the Manufacturing Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI) has been contracting for seven straight months; and the Consumer Price Index (CPI) has once again reached the “300s” range… Recently, the Taiwanese authorities have released the economic data for January 2023.
Experts say that Taiwan’s economy is underperforming in the new year and growth pressures are mounting.
According to the financial authorities in Taiwan, the region's exports in January this year amounted to 31.51 billion US dollars, a year-on-year decrease of 21.2%, marking the fifth consecutive month of negative growth.
Exports in all 11 major export categories declined compared to the same period last year.
Plastics, rubber and their products, as well as optical equipment, experienced the largest declines, with annual reductions of 37.6% and 35.7% respectively.
The annual export of electronic components decreased by 20.1%, marking the largest decline in 11 years.
Among them, the annual decline in integrated circuits was 18.3%, representing the largest decrease in 14 years.
Cai Meina, the head of the statistics department at that ministry, stated that this indicates the spread of the weak demand effects within the consumer electronics industry, and that the electronics sector has entered a period of adjustment.
Statistics show that in January, both imports and exports in Taiwan region declined. The trade surplus amounted to only $2.34 billion, the lowest level in nearly three years.
The financial authorities in Taiwan believe that the decline in global final demand, along with industrial adjustments and inventory reductions, are discouraging manufacturers from purchasing materials. As a result, the worsening situation in exports is unlikely to improve in the short term. Taiwan's export performance in the first quarter of this year is expected to decline more severely than anticipated.
According to the Taiwan China Economic Research Institute, the seasonally adjusted Manufacturing Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI) for Taiwan in January this year was 40.4%, a further decline of 3.3 percentage points from December last year, marking the seventh consecutive month of contraction.
In the economic monitoring indicator system, the PMI uses 50% as the dividing line between expansion and contraction. An index value above 50% indicates economic expansion, while a value below 50% indicates economic contraction.
Among the five components of the Taiwan PMI in January, there was a contraction in new orders, production, and employment levels; supplier delivery times decreased, and inventory levels also tightened.
The six major industries that reported PMI contraction were: electrical power and mechanical equipment (35.1%), electronics and optics (35.2%), chemicals and biotechnology and medical (39.2%), basic raw materials (42.4%), transportation (42.6%) and food and textiles (45.7%).
Regarding prices, the Taiwan authorities’ “General Accounting Office” announced that the annual inflation rate in Taiwan in January this year was 3.04%, once again exceeding 3% for the first time since July last year.
Among them, vegetables rose by 28.25 per cent, a new 17-month high.
Cao Zhihong, a special commissioner from Taiwan’s “General Accounting Office,” frankly stated that the increase in vegetable prices has indeed exceeded expectations. Excluding the impact of the Spring Festival, the average CPI for January and February this year should be close to 2.71% in December last year. Inflationary pressures still exist and remain at a high level.
Looking ahead to this year’s Taiwanese economy, experts are pessimistic, based on reports from local media sources such as the United Daily and Yahoo Finance.
Wu Dajin, a professor of economics at Taiwan’s Central University, analyzes that the export downturn may cause cash flow problems for export-oriented manufacturers and raise the risk of debt default.
At the same time, declining orders have forced manufacturers to cut labor costs, which in turn affects the labor market and household incomes, thereby undermining consumer spending power.
Qiu Dasheng, a researcher at the Taiwan Institute of Economic Research, believes that the inflation problems in Europe and the United States have not been resolved this year, and demand continues to decline. He predicts that Taiwan’s export slump will persist throughout the first half of the year.
Since Taiwan's economy is supported by exports, the annual economic growth will be weaker than last year due to the sluggish performance of exports.
Did the Balloon Incident Brighten America's Eyes?
Strengthening restrictions on technology exports to China
According to a report in The Wall Street Journal today, following the balloon incident, the United States is preparing to further tighten restrictions on the export of technology to China.
Current and former security officials have stated that the aforementioned balloon incident highlights the national security threat posed by China, and will help gain more political support for strengthening America’s technological defenses.
The United States claimed that the balloon carried antennas and sensors for intelligence collection and communication.
According to Martijn Rasser, a former senior official of the US Central Intelligence Agency who now works at the Washington-based think tank New American Security Center:
“This is undoubtedly adding fuel to the fire, supporting the views of those who take a tough stance towards China.”
“We will also consider taking more extensive action to expose and respond to China’s larger-scale surveillance activities that pose a threat to our national security and to our allies and partners,” White House Press Secretary Karine Jean-Pierre told reporters on Thursday.
US officials said they had informed more than 30 governments about the balloon incident, and that international coordination was crucial to address the Chinese threat.
Emily Benso, a senior researcher at the Center for Strategic and International Studies, said that in addition to the actions of the Biden administration, the newly established U.S. House Committee on Strategic Competition with the Communist Party of China could also exert pressure on the United States to take more stringent measures to slow down China’s development.
She said that members of Congress will face increasing pressure to take a more aggressive stance, which in turn may force the White House to adopt even more stringent policies.
The Wall Street Journal reports that many advocates for stricter export controls are also pushing to expand the scope of these controls to include industries such as artificial intelligence.
The US government has also been developing an outward investment review program to examine whether US investments abroad pose potential national security threats from China.
Analysts say the White House may face calls for a faster launch of the plan.
The first individual pension products have been launched, with minimum holding period of 360 days - Xinhua News Agency
The first batch of personal pension financial products is now on sale.
There are 7 products available from this domestic institution to choose from, and the minimum holding period is only 360 days.
The personal pension financial products have finally been launched.
On February 10, China Financial Network released the first list of personal pension financial products, seven of the personal pension financial products of the Industrial Bank of China, the Agricultural Bank of China and the Postal Bank of China were officially released.
The “shelf” of personal pension accounts now includes four types of products: personal pension savings, personal pension financing, personal pension insurance, and personal pension public fund.
According to the information provided, the first batch of personal pension financial products are all publicly offered, net-value, open-ended products. There are 5 newly issued products and 2 existing products. With the exception of one product which is a hybrid type, the remaining 6 products are all fixed-income products.
The Beijing Youth Daily reporter noted that out of five new products launched, four were from ICBC Asset Management, all being fixed income products with varying shortest holding periods ranging from 365 days to 1080 days, and their corresponding performance benchmarks (annualized) were as follows: 3.70% - 4.20%, 4.10% - 4.60%, 4.40% - 4.90%, and 5.25% - 5.75%.
The remaining new product is “Youyin Fortune Tianyi·Hongjin Minimum Holding Period of 1095 Days No. 1,” which is also a fixed-income product. The fundraising for this product began on February 10 and ended on February 19, with a risk rating of Level 2.
Of the two remaining products, one is the Agricultural Bank of China’s financial product “Agricultural Bank of China Tongxin·Lingdong” 360-Day Technology Innovation RMB Financial Product, which has a mixed investment nature and a risk level of three.
The other ongoing product is “Youyin Fortune Tianyi·Hongjin Minimum Holding Period of 365 Days No. 1,” which is a fixed-income type. It began fundraising on December 30 last year and officially started operating on January 4 this year. As of February 8, its cumulative net value was 1.0011.
According to the State Council Office's Opinion on Promoting the Development of Personal Pensions, the funds of the personal pension fund account can be invested in financial products such as bank accounts, savings deposits, commercial pension insurance, public equity funds, etc.
The launch of the first batch of personal pension financial products marks the official commencement of the ability for individual pension investors to purchase financial products through their personal pension fund accounts.
Last November, the China Banking and Insurance Regulatory Commission (CBIRC) formulated the "Interim Measures for the Management of Personal Pension Business by Commercial Banks and Financial Planning Companies."
The Scheme provides that participants may purchase personal pension products such as personal retirement savings, personal retirement financial products, personal retirement insurance products, and personal retirement public fund products through the personal retirement fund account.
Subsequently, three departments—the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security, the Ministry of Finance, and the State Taxation Administration—issued a notice clarifying that the individual pension system is to be implemented in 36 pilot cities and regions, including Beijing, Tianjin, Shijiazhuang in Hebei Province, Xiongan New Area, and Jincheng in Shanxi Province.
As of December 31, 2022, there were 19.5 million participants in personal pension plans, with 6.13 million individuals contributing to them and total contributions amounting to RMB 1.42 billion.
Previously, the banks participating in the pilot had only listed three types of products: personal pension savings, personal pension insurance products and personal pension public funds.
Now that all the personal pension investment products are available, how should investors make their choices?
Experts from the Jilin Bank Product Development Department said that compared with other personal pension products, both pilot-stage pension-linked wealth management products and individual pension-linked wealth management products have three characteristics.
The first aspect is robustness: the risk management mechanisms have been improved, investment strategies and philosophies have become more prudent, and third-party independent custody is implemented by entities other than the parent bank.
The second aspect is the long-term nature: during the pilot phase, the duration of pension financial products was set at 5 years or more. For the personal pension financial products to be issued in the next step, the minimum holding period will be 1 year, with an encouragement to hold them for more than 3 years.
The third aspect is inclusivity: the threshold for purchasing products is low, with a minimum purchase amount generally being 1 yuan, and in some cases, it can be as low as 0.01 yuan. Additionally, the fees for product custody and management are more favorable.
Experts point out that investors should make their choices based on the characteristics of the products and their own risk tolerance.
Personal pension savings are characterized by long maturity periods, high interest rates, and high safety levels, making them suitable for individuals with a low risk tolerance. Personal pension insurance products focus on providing protection and are more appropriate for those who cannot afford to take on investment risks but are willing to accept stable returns. On the other hand, personal pension investment products and publicly offered fund products do not guarantee the principal or returns; they carry certain investment risks but offer higher expected returns, making them suitable for individuals with some financial knowledge and a higher risk tolerance.
Article/Reporter: Cheng Jie; Coordination: Chai Hua Bo
Seminar for Newly Appointed Members and Alternates of the Central Committee, as Well as Key Provincial and Ministerial Leaders, on Studying and Implementing Xi Jinping's Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the Spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China Concludes – Rolling News – Hunan Daily Online – Huasheng Online
The seminar for newly appointed members and alternate members of the Central Committee, as well as key leading cadres at the provincial and ministerial levels, to study and implement Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China has concluded.
2023-02-11 13:07:20 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Xufeng] Font size: [Large, Medium, Small]
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10th: A seminar for newly appointed members of the Central Committee, alternate members of the Central Committee, and key leading cadres at the provincial and ministerial levels to study and implement Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China concluded on the afternoon of the 10th at the Central Party School (National Academy of Governance). Cai Qi, a member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Secretary of the Secretariat of the CPC Central Committee, attended the closing ceremony and delivered a concluding speech.
He said that the Chinese people should learn in depth from the spirit of the important speech of General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar, more firmly uphold the principle of "two establishments" and firmly do the "two defences", strengthen their skills, take serious action, and firmly advance the work of Chinese-style modernization, and achieve results that can be tested by history, practice and the people in the comprehensive construction of a socialist modernized state and the comprehensive promotion of the great revival of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar, all participants were guided by Xi Jinping's ideas of socialism with Chinese characteristics in the new era, carefully studied the spirit of the 20th Party Congress and the important speech of the General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar, and engaged in in-depth discussions and exchanges in connection with practical activities. They deepened their understanding of a series of major theoretical and practical issues of Chinese-style modernization, strengthened their confidence and determination to comprehensively advance the great revival of the Chinese nation with Chinese-style modernization under the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee, with Comrade Xi Jinping as its core, and strengthened their sense of responsibility and mission to fulfil their duties, do their work well and ensure a good start to the new era.
At the closing ceremony, 10 workshop delegates made presentations and shared their learnings.
Cai Qi stated that studying and implementing the thought of Xi Jinping on socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China is not only the primary political task at present and for some time to come, but also a long-term strategic task. It is necessary to follow the requirements of “comprehensive learning, comprehensive understanding, and comprehensive implementation” to ensure that the work of study and implementation continues to deepen, become more practical, and take root in people’s minds.
To more profoundly understand the decisive significance of the “two establishments,” we must resolutely uphold General Secretary Xi Jinping’s core position, as well as the authority and centralized, unified leadership of the Central Committee of the Party. We must continuously enhance our political judgment, understanding, and execution capabilities, and always maintain a high degree of consistency in our thoughts, politics, and actions with the Central Committee of the Party, with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core.
We must strive to master the theory of Marxism as our core competence, and consciously use the Party’s innovative theories to arm our minds, guide our practice, and advance our work. We need to put effort into in-depth study, careful comprehension, and earnest application of these theories, in order to truly develop firm beliefs, absolute loyalty, and a sense of mission and responsibility.
We must implement the various decisions and arrangements of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with a spirit of diligence and initiative, steadily advance China's path to modernization, roll up our sleeves and work hard, and take on the role of "construction team leaders" to turn the blueprint into reality step by step.
It must be remembered that the comprehensive and strict governance of the Party is an ongoing process, as is the Party’s self-revolution. We must firmly uphold the political responsibilities associated with this governance, taking the Party’s political construction as the guiding principle, and vigorously advance the new great project of Party building in the new era.
It is necessary to enhance the capabilities to promote high-quality development, to serve the people, and to prevent and resolve risks. We must foster a strong culture of investigation and research, and resolutely prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucracy.
Shi Taifeng, Li Ganjie, Li Shulei, Chen Wenqing, Liu Jingguo, and Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony, which was presided over by Chen Xi.
The last communist prime minister of East Germany has passed away today.
The successor of the East German Communist Party reported in a party statement, “Last night, Hans Modrow left us at the age of 95.
Our party has thus lost an important leader.
‘
On November 13, 1989, four days after the fall of the Berlin Wall that had separated East Berlin from West Berlin for 28 years, Modrow stated that he would help transform East Germany into a democratic country.
At that time, the Communist Party leaders were forced to step down as protesters across East Germany demanded democracy and freedom.
When Mikhail Gorbachev came to power in the Soviet Union, he called for change in Soviet-dominated Eastern Europe.
In March 1990, Modrow announced the first and only free elections in the German Democratic Republic (GDR).
The results of the election led to his removal from the position of Prime Minister.
Despite the reforms implemented by Modrow, his opponents accused him of trying to delay the political changes and reunification that took place in October 1990.
He has also been criticized for attempting to restructure the secret police rather than abolish it.
In 1993, Modrow was found guilty of election fraud in the municipal elections of May 1989, but he was not imprisoned.
These allegations were allegedly politically motivated.
From 1990 to 1994, Modrow continued to serve in the German parliament, and from 1999 to 2004, he was a member of the European Parliament.
Modrow sees himself as a reformer and hopes to change the Communist Party from within.
In 1999, he told Reuters that he did not want the return of the old East Germany, but that East Germany’s achievements should be recognized.
Modrow was born in 1928 in the then German town of Jasenitz (now Jasienica in Poland) and trained as a mechanic.
During World War II, he served as the leader of a youth fire brigade and, towards the end of the conflict, became a member of the Nazi militia Volkssturm, which recruited men aged 16 to 60 to join the final struggles of the war.
At the age of 17, Modrow was captured by the Soviet army and taken as a prisoner of war to the Soviet Union, where he attended anti-Fascist courses and became a committed Communist.
In 1949, the year East Germany was established, he returned to his home country and found a job as a mechanic. He continued to study social sciences and economics, and later obtained a doctorate degree.
Modrow was a staff member of the Free German Youth Movement, which almost all East German youth joined, and was promoted to the position of president of the Dresden Regional Party from 1973 to 1989 through the ruling Social Democratic Union Party (SED).
He also served in the East German parliament for more than 30 years.
In 1990, Modrow became the de facto leader of East Germany and held the highest state office.
Vietnam News Agency, Hanoi – A special correspondent from the Vietnam News Agency reports that the official visit of Vietnamese Prime Minister Phan Minh Chinh and his spouse to Singapore and Brunei has been a complete success, yielding comprehensive, practical, and concrete results.
During his three-day visit to Singapore and Brunei, Prime Minister Phan Minh Chinh participated in more than 30 different events.
The results achieved have given new impetus to the ongoing development of the Viet Nam-New Zealand strategic partnership and the Vietnamese-New Zealand comprehensive partnership in a deeper, broader and more effective direction.
During his visits to both countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Triet continued to reaffirm the foreign policy of the Vietnamese Party and the State, namely, independence, autonomy, pluralism, diversity, willingness to be a good friend and reliable partner of all countries and a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is in the interests of both countries, as it contributes to the well-being of their respective peoples and to regional and global peace, stability, and development.
During various meetings and talks, Prime Minister Phan Minh Chinh and the leaders of Singapore and Brunei unanimously agreed to continuously enhance political mutual trust with Vietnam through reciprocal visits by high-level delegations, the effective implementation of various bilateral cooperation mechanisms, and the signing of important cooperation agreements.
Many cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among these, two major highlights include the Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei Darussalam for the 2023-2027 Period.
Viet Nam signed a Memorandum of Understanding on a Green and Digital Economy Partnership with Singapore.
Image from VNA.
During meetings with business leaders, colloquia and economic forums, Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet stressed that Viet Nam welcomes and facilitates the expansion of investments by Singaporean and Bruneian companies in the fields of digital transformation, green energy, high technology, innovative ideas and other areas in Viet Nam.
The visit not only helped to deepen Viet Nam &apos; s cooperation with Singapore and Brunei in various traditional areas of politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defence, education and training, oil and gas, tourism, civil exchanges, etc., but also created a framework for cooperation between the countries in new potential areas such as digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovative ideas, smart cities, sustainable development, etc.
King Hassanal Bolkiah of Brunei and Prime Minister Phan Mạnh Quỳnh are preparing to enter into bilateral talks.
Image from VNA.
During his visits to both countries, Prime Minister Phan Minh Chinh made time to meet with and listen to the concerns and aspirations of the Vietnamese communities living there.
During the meetings between the two leaders, Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet recommended that the authorities of both countries pay more attention to and create favourable conditions for the local Vietnamese community to be treated fairly, to have the opportunity to contribute to local society and to foster bilateral relations.
Both suggestions were agreed upon and supported by the leaders of the two countries.
In particular, Prime Minister Fan Mingzheng also shared with the leaders of both countries the desire for a cohesive, peaceful, stable, and prosperous ASEAN community. They agreed unanimously to maintain unity and cooperation with ASEAN countries and to enhance ASEAN’s central role in the context of the complex and dynamic regional and international situations.
Thanks to the important achievements made, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh’s official visits to Singapore and Brunei have made a positive contribution to the effective implementation of the Communist Party of Vietnam (CPV)’s foreign policy priorities as outlined at the 13th National Congress of the CPV, which focus on strengthening relations with ASEAN neighbors. These visits have also aided in the effective execution of Conclusion No. 12-KL/TW of the CPV Central Committee’s Political Bureau regarding the work of Vietnamese expatriates under the new circumstances, as well as in leveraging the strength of the entire national unity.
(continued)
NEWS GOV-MO: Police announcement: Police Department calls on citizens to beware of fake telecom companies scam text messages
Recently, the Police Bureau received multiple reports of telecommunications fraud cases where criminals impersonated local telecom companies and sent fraudulent SMSs containing links to fake websites, promising rewards for exchanging points that were about to expire.
The victim followed the instructions and entered their credit card information and verification code. Shortly thereafter, they received a notice from the financial institution stating that there were unauthorized transactions on their credit card, leading them to suspect that their credit card details had been stolen through the aforementioned website.
The investigation confirmed that the telecommunications company concerned had not sent the aforementioned text message.
The police department is urging citizens to be vigilant if they receive similar text messages on their mobile phones. They should not click on the links contained in the messages or provide any personal information. If they are asked to provide credit card details, account transaction passwords, or transaction verification codes, they should be especially cautious to prevent their credit cards from being fraudulently used.
Anti-scam tips:
1. Pay more attention to cybersecurity news and enhance personal awareness of prevention.
2. Never log in to websites of unknown origin, and do not provide personal or credit card information on such websites to prevent it from being misused by others.
3. Be wary of fake websites and phishing sites, and always check whether the website address matches the official website address exactly.
4. Install antivirus software on your mobile phone, mobile device, or computer, and update it regularly.
If you suspect that you have been a victim of fraud or any other crime, please contact the Police Commissioner's Fraud Reporting Hotline at 8800 7777 or the Crime Report Line at 993 for assistance immediately.
EU summit debates refugee policy, EU officials: reception process is a bottleneck - China News Network
The EU summit was marked by intense arguments over refugee policies, with EU officials stating that there are bottlenecks at every step of the reception process.
【Global Times correspondent in Belgium, Niu Ruifei】According to a report by AFP on February 10, at the latest EU summit of that day, EU Commission President Ursula von der Leyen stated that EU leaders agreed to adopt stricter policies regarding illegal immigration in order to make it easier to deport such individuals.
The EU’s move is reportedly in response to growing concerns about illegal immigration in Europe, where the core problem today is that few illegal migrants are eventually repatriated.
According to the summit document, EU leaders called on the Commission to “immediately mobilize substantial EU funds” to strengthen external borders through infrastructure and surveillance.
However, the EU and its member states have been constantly arguing over issues such as the payment for the construction of the fences.
Von der Leyen has repeatedly stated that EU funds will not cover the costs involved.
However, diplomats from some member states have stated that if the EU could share the cost of installing cameras, watchtowers, and other infrastructure along the external borders, it would free up national budgets, thereby accelerating the construction process.
According to the European Euractiv website, EU officials have admitted that bottlenecks exist at every step of the refugee reception process, that limited reception capacity and overburdened immigration authorities in member states cannot prevent refugees from filing “numerous” asylum applications across the EU, and that the EU’s reception system is in an almost “eternal crisis.”
The European Commission estimates that in 2017, EU Schengen countries received over 920,000 asylum applications, up nearly half from the previous year.
Meanwhile, the EU recorded more than 330,000 illegal entry cases last year.
In this context, the summit also reached an agreement on a “principle” according to which EU countries may return illegal immigrants to their home country based on a court judgment from another member state.
In addition, EU leaders reportedly agreed to “increase the use of the concept of safe states,” which would pave the way for the EU to develop a common list.
(Source: Global Times; Author: Liu Ruifei)
Xia Liyan, Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang, visited China to convey Song Tao’s message: Under the 1992 Consensus, visits from the Green Movement to the Chinese mainland are welcome.
Hsieh Li-yen, the vice chairman of the Kuomintang (KMT) in Taiwan, met with Song Tao, the director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of China, and Wang Huning, a member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of China (CPC), during his recent visit to China.
Zhao Chunshan, a senior advisor to the Kuomintang’s official organization, the National Policy Foundation, was interviewed by Taiwan Central News Agency last night. He gave a positive response to what Song Tao said regarding Hsieh Li-yen: as long as people agree with the “1992 Consensus” and oppose Taiwan independence, China welcomes people from the Green Movement to visit the Chinese mainland.
The National Party has considered it a fresh development.
Xia Liyan met with Song Tao earlier that day, but the news did not mention this claim.
The ruling Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) in Taiwan has repeatedly clarified that it refuses to accept the '1992 Consensus'.
According to Xinhua News Agency today, Hsieh Li-yen, the vice chairman of the Kuomintang, led a delegation on a visit to the Chinese mainland. During his stay in Beijing, he met with Wang Huning, a member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, the newly appointed Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, Song Tao, and Yin Li, the secretary of the Beijing Municipal Party Committee.
In an interview with Song Tao, Xi Liyen said that the political basis of the Communist Party of China was the "Consensus of 92" and anti-Taiwan independence, while Zhao Chunshan, a senior adviser to the Nationalist Party's State Policy Foundation, said that the Nationalist Party's "Consensus of 92" was the true "Consensus of 92".
Zhao Chunshan notes that this is different from his previous experiences at meetings.
During recent video discussions with scholars from the Chinese mainland, as well as this particular discussion, I did not hear any scholars discussing the topic of military unification or the “Anti-Secession Law.” Instead, the focus was on the restoration of exchanges and dialogue.
Zhao Chunshan pointed out that the situation across the Taiwan Strait is one of hostility and danger, and the Chinese mainland hopes to convey its desire to improve relations through the Kuomintang.
Because there is no mutual trust between the CPC and the other party, the latter is still willing to work well for the Taiwanese, and the delegate does not want to damage relations between the two sides.
According to Zhao Chunshan, Wang Huning also personally gave instructions, telling Song Tao, “The demands made by them (Taiwanese farmers and fishermen) must be fulfilled. If it’s not possible to resolve the issue comprehensively, then individual cases should be dealt with on a case-by-case basis.”
The report did not mention whether the Nationalist Party delegation visiting the mainland directly referred to the daily overflights of Chinese military aircraft and warships, the agricultural and fisheries problems in Taiwan's few counties and cities, or whether the Central News Agency reporters were interviewed to raise such issues.
What exactly was that “object” that was shot down over Alaska?
Confusing and full of speculation
On Friday afternoon (February 10), the U.S. military once again utilized its most advanced stealth jet fighter, the F-22, to shoot down an unidentified object that was flying over Alaska.
The location where it was downed is ten miles from the coast of Alaska.
This is the second time in less than a week that the U.S. military has shot down an object flying in the air.
Last Saturday, a spy balloon from China was shot down off the coast of South Carolina, several days after drifting over US airspace.
The Pentagon stated that the second object that was shot down first entered U.S. airspace on Thursday evening and was tracked by the U.S. military as it moved over northeastern Alaska at an altitude of 12,000 meters (40,000 feet). Its size was comparable to that of a small car, making it much smaller than the previous Chinese spy balloon that had been shot down.
The Pentagon still believes that there is no evidence to suggest that this object can be controlled.
John Corby, the White House National Security Council's Strategic Communications Coordinator, said on Friday that while the exact appearance of the high-altitude object was not clear, it "posed a reasonable threat to the safety of civil aviation."
Kobe said that this object is different from the spy balloon discovered in the United States, which does not have an attached payload.
Kobe said, “Calling it an ‘object’ is the best description we have at the moment.”
President Biden listened to the Pentagon’s advice before ordering the object to be shot down, and he was “very careful” in making that decision, Corby added.
The United States official description of the object can be summarized roughly as: the size of a small car, without joysticks, without suspension, flying at an altitude of about 10,000 metres.
But these data do not answer basic questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what mission it is performing.
Many analyses and speculations on the Internet now suggest that this may be another Chinese balloon.
It may have come from China, as did the spy balloon that invaded US airspace and the Chinese balloon that hovered over Latin America, both of which were performing a mission in different locations.
And some have linked this “object” in Alaska to UFOs.
A report in Newsweek cited a tweet posted by former U.S. Representative Peter Meijer on Twitter on Friday, which read: “I really hope this ‘unidentified flying object’ turns out to be a spy balloon, rather than a legitimate UFO.”
The irony of conflating extraterrestrial spacecraft with weather balloons is striking, but it does not warrant an interstellar conflict, he said.
Mager posted this tweet shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object in Alaska had been shot down.
The Newsweek said that it was not only Mejer who suspected the object was a UFO.
Tim Burchett, a Republican congressman from Tennessee, criticized the government's attempt to conceal information last month and called on the Office of the Director of National Intelligence (DNI) to release reports regarding unidentified flying objects (UFOs).
Xi Jinping replies in a letter, encouraging members of the Chinese medical team aiding Africa to bring benefits to the local people with kindness and expertise, and to tell China’s story through practical actions – Rolling News – Hunan Daily Online – Huasheng Online
Xi Jinping replied in a letter, encouraging the members of the Chinese medical team aiding China and Africa to bring benefits to the local people with kindness and professional skills, and to tell China’s story well through their practical actions.
2023-02-11 13:09:10 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Xufeng] Font size: [Large, Medium, Small]
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10th: Xi Jinping, General Secretary of the Communist Party of China (CPC), President of the People’s Republic of China, and Chairman of the Central Military Commission, replied on February 9th to the members of the 19th batch of Chinese medical teams dispatched to assist the Central African Republic. He extended greetings to them and to all medical personnel involved in international aid efforts, and expressed his earnest hopes for their work.
In his reply, Xi Jinping said: "You have overcome the difficulties in your work and life in China and Africa, and you have dedicated yourselves to serving the local people. You are not only angels in white who save lives and heal the wounded, but also friendly envoys who convey goodwill."
This year marks the 60th anniversary of China’s dispatching medical teams abroad; I extend sincere greetings to all comrades who have and continue to serve in international medical missions.
Xi Jinping stated that the Chinese people love peace and cherish life, and medical aid to other countries is a vivid manifestation of this.
I hope that you will never forget your original aspirations and always keep your mission in mind. You should vigorously promote the spirit of the Chinese medical team, which is characterized by fearlessness in the face of difficulties, willingness to contribute, a commitment to saving lives and healing the wounded, and boundless compassion. Bring benefits to the local people with kindness and medical expertise, and tell China’s story through concrete actions. Make even greater contributions to promoting the establishment of a global community for human health and well-being.
Medical assistance to other countries is an important part of our foreign aid efforts.
In 1963, our country sent its first medical team abroad to Algeria for assistance.
Over the past 60 years, a total of 30,000 medical personnel have been dispatched to 76 countries and regions in Africa, Asia, the Americas, Europe, and Oceania. They have treated 290 million patients, earning widespread praise from the international community.
Currently, the foreign aid medical teams are working at 115 medical facilities in 56 countries around the world, with nearly half of them located in remote and difficult areas.
Recently, 11 members of the 19th Chinese medical team dispatched to Central Africa wrote a letter to General Secretary Xi Jinping, reporting on their efforts to study and implement the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, as well as on providing medical services to the local population. They expressed their determination to contribute to the establishment of a global community for human health and well-being.
Iran is commemorating the anniversary of its revolution; hackers supporting the protests hacked the president’s televised speech.
The Islamic Republic of Iran held an official rally on Saturday to mark the 44th anniversary of the Iranian revolution, but anti-government hackers briefly interrupted President Ibrahim Raisi’s television address.
The president’s live television speech was interrupted for about a minute on the internet; during that time, a logo belonging to a group of anti-Iranian hackers appeared on the screen. The hackers are known as “Edalat Ali (Ali of Justice)”.
A voice also appeared shouting "Death to the Islamic Republic".
According to a report by Reuters today, as Iran marked the anniversary of its revolution, hackers interrupted the broadcasts of the national television station.
As Iran officially commemorates the 44th anniversary of the Iranian revolution, Raisi’s hardline government faces the boldest challenge from young protesters who are calling for its ouster, but Raisi still calls on “deceived youth” to repent so that they can be pardoned by Iran’s supreme leader.
National protests continue in Iran after the death of 22-year-old Mahsa Amini in September while in custody of the country’s moral police.
The Iranian security forces’ deadly crackdown on protests is one of the strongest challenges the Islamic Republic has faced since the 1979 revolution overthrew the 2,500-year-old monarchy.
As part of an amnesty commemorating the anniversary of the revolution, Iranian authorities released on Friday the imprisoned dissident Farhad Mesami, who was on a hunger strike, as well as the Iranian-French scholar Fariba Adelha.
Earlier, Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei issued an amnesty that included some of the prisoners arrested during recent anti-government protests.
According to a report by the human rights organization HRANA, as of Friday, 528 protesters had been killed, including 71 minors.
The report also states that 70 government security personnel were killed.
It is believed that as many as 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For several weeks, Iranian leaders and official media have been calling for a vote to take place at the gathering on Saturday, in order to demonstrate opposition to the protests and support for the government.
On the evening of the anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, on Friday night, official media showed fireworks as part of government-sponsored celebration events. People shouted “Allahu Akbar!”
(God is greatest!)".
However, at the gathering, it was also possible to hear many people shouting, “Die, dictator!”
“And the phrase ‘Death of the Islamic Republic’ that appears in the videos posted on social media.”
On Saturday, the government television station broadcast live videos of official gatherings in various states across the country.
In Tehran, as part of the official celebrations, domestically produced anti-ballistic missiles, drones, anti-submarine cruisers and other military equipment were displayed.
President Lacey’s speeches were often interrupted by the slogan “America, die!”, which has become a symbol of these state rallies.
The crowd also shouted "Death to Israel".
According to Reuters, Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019, is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran. This is one of the factors that have contributed to the deterioration of relations between Paris and Tehran in recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison in 2020 for national security offences.
They later placed her under house arrest, but in January she returned to prison.
Adelkhah denied these allegations.
A week before his release, Mesami’s supporters warned that he was at risk of death as a result of his hunger strike protests.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting the mandatory wearing of headscarves.
The French Foreign Ministry called for Adelkhah’s release on Friday, calling for her freedom to be restored, “including her being allowed to return to France if she so wishes.”
‘
The Sixteenth China-Japan Energy and Environmental Comprehensive Forum was held in Beijing; He Li Feng attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech - Xinhua News Agency
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 11 – On February 11, the 16th China-Japan Comprehensive Forum on Energy Conservation and Environmental Protection was held in Beijing, combining both online and offline formats.
He Lifeng, a member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the National Development and Reform Commission, attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech.
Huang Lifeng noted that hosting this forum is an important step in implementing the consensus reached at the joint meeting between President Xi Jinping and Prime Minister Fumio Kishida in Bangkok to strengthen green development cooperation between China and Japan.
China will fully implement the spirit of the 20th Congress of the Communist Party of China, accelerate the green transformation of development methods, make great strides in combating environmental pollution, comprehensively strengthen resource conservation, actively and steadily promote carbon neutrality to the highest level, and promote carbon reduction, pollution reduction, greening and growth in synergy, as well as ecological priority, energy-efficiency and green low-carbon development.
China is willing to work with Japan to further deepen cooperation in green and low-carbon industries, technological exchanges, policy dialogue, and cultural interactions, thereby promoting the advancement of bilateral cooperation on green development to new levels.
Japanese Minister of Economy, Trade and Industry, Yasuhiro Nishimura, attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech.
The forum is jointly organized by the National Development and Reform Commission of China, the Ministry of Commerce of China, the Ministry of Economy and Trade of Japan, and the Japanese-Chinese Economic Association, featuring a main forum and four sub-forums on energy efficiency improvement, automotive electrification and automation, hydrogen energy, and long-term trade between China and Japan.
Representatives of Chinese and Japanese governments, enterprises and institutions exchanged views.
Chongyang Q&A: How to View the Surprising Strength of January’s Non-Farm Employment Data in the US and Its Future Trends – Economic Observation Network, a Professional Financial News Website
Q: Regarding Chongyang Investment, how do they view the significantly better-than-expected non-farm employment data in the United States in January and the future trends?
On February 3, the U.S. Department of Labor released the non-farm employment data for January 2023. The number of new non-farm jobs created was 517,000, significantly higher than the market expectation of 189,000; the unemployment rate dropped to 3.4%, the lowest level in nearly 50 years; the hourly wage growth rate increased by 4.4% year-on-year and by 0.3% month-on-month, showing a slight slowdown.
Overall, there are many one-time and technical factors that have influenced these numbers, such as teachers and staff returning to work after strikes, adjustments to the survey methodology, and updates to seasonal adjustment factors. Subsequent revisions may be made (for example, in January 2022, the number of non-farm jobs was revised downward from 504,000 to 364,000), indicating that non-farm employment may not be as strong as the data suggests.
Structurally, the impact of layoffs in high-tech enterprises remains, but is relatively low; new employment in high-contact services such as leisure hotels, education and health care has recovered significantly, and data show that the labour force gap in services remains.
Combined with the rebound in data on the service sector PMI (which also exceeded expectations), as well as data on job vacancies and labor shortages, and the strong performance of consumer credit figures, we conclude that the U.S. service sector has experienced a rapid recovery following the extreme weather and holiday periods.
We believe that supply-demand tensions in the US job market will hardly improve without a recession.
Currently, there is still a supply gap of over 5 million in US labor markets, with labor participation rates rising slowly, especially among those aged 25 to 54 who have already reached their pre-pandemic peak.
In addition, due to the high levels of excess savings among U.S. residents and the strong performance of consumer credit, the strong demand for consumption will further delay the impact of austerity policies on the job market.
The ongoing tight supply and demand in the U.S. job market will be a defining feature of the U.S. economy in 2023.
With the upcoming end of the interest rate hike cycle and the continuous fluctuations in inflation expectations, we are not optimistic about the continued decline in wage growth.
Before this data was released, US equity-bond markets were overly optimistic about the Fed’s rate-hiking path.
As inflation data continues to improve, the Fed is slowing its rate hikes while maintaining a fragile balance of market inflation expectations. But markets are ignoring the Fed’s hawk-like statements, expecting not only an early halt to the hikes, but two rate cuts at the end of the year.
In a situation where the supply and demand in the labor market are tight, and the effects of austerity policies are uncertain, we believe that the Federal Reserve’s guidance on interest rate hikes at the end of the year is relatively reasonable. However, adjustments to market expectations that are too extreme, as well as overcrowding in trading activities, could potentially cause some harm to the market.
However, the persistence of wage growth will not reverse the current rapidly declining trend in inflation. As M2 data turns negative year-on-year and the leading indicators of the various CPI sub-elements gradually improve, the US CPI data has moved into a rapidly declining phase since October, the persistence of wage growth will only form a base for future inflation data, and the current market expectations are difficult to falsify, and the market will enter a new round of play after the next inflation data is released.
Shenzhen: Building the First and World's Leading High-Speed City-China News Network
Xinhua News Agency reported on February 11th that the Shenzhen Industrial and Information Technology Bureau has recently issued the “Action Plan for Building an Ultra-fast Pioneer City of Shenzhen”.
It is proposed that by the end of 2023, a super broadband network with high rates, large capacity, and low latency will be built to achieve the goal of “Dual Gigabit, Full Optical Network, 1 millisecond, Everything Connected,” making it China’s first and world-leading city in terms of ultra-fast speed.
The plan calls for accelerating the upgrade of the gigabit optical network.
By the end of 2023, the proportion of 10G PON ports will reach 100%, and the number of all-optical industrial parks (business parks) will exceed 100.
The plan calls for an overall improvement in 5G network efficiency.
Research and develop standards for the quality of service of Shenzhen’s 5G networks, conduct 5G network testing and evaluation, and improve the overall quality of 5G network services.
Supports basic telecommunications companies in enhancing the optimization of 5G networks in key areas and locations. An additional 10,000 5G base stations will be installed throughout the year, resulting in an average download speed of 500 Mbps and an upload speed of 100 Mbps across the city. In key areas, the download speed will reach 1000 Mbps, and the upload speed will reach 200 Mbps, significantly improving both network performance and user experience.
Build a city-level high-quality wireless local area network.
Develop service specifications for wireless local area network (WLAN) in public places, promote the upgrade of WLAN systems in densely populated areas and regions with high information consumption demands across all districts of the city, and provide gigabit access capabilities.
Relying on the “Shen-i Network,” a unified authentication and supervision platform for the city’s public wireless local area networks is established to achieve “one-time authentication, seamless roaming, and intelligent switching.” This platform also supports operators in incorporating self-built APs (wireless access points) from the community that provide public services into the authentication and supervision system.
By the end of 2023, the total number of upgraded access points will be no less than 20,000.
In addition, the Plan proposes to build high-quality all-optical carrier networks, build multi-tier computing power supply systems, accelerate the construction of key communications network facilities and improve the capacity of Internet application services.
The “Plan” clearly states the need to collaboratively establish an IoT (Internet of Things) perception system.
Explore the establishment of a management model for urban perception terminals based on the “open-source HarmonyOS” operating system, reduce integration costs, accelerate the construction of city-level IoT (Internet of Things) perception platforms, and promote interconnection and data sharing between the urban IoT platforms and specialized IoT platforms in various fields.
Deepen the application of IoT (Internet of Things) technologies in areas such as urban management, public services, public safety, and transportation. Expand the channels for data collection, including both fixed sensors located on urban roads, buildings, and public facilities, as well as mobile sensors from intelligent connected vehicles.
By the end of 2023, the number of IoT sensing terminals for water, electricity, and gas will exceed 9 million, with 20 demonstration projects for the application of multi-functional intelligent poles being established.
The plan also noted that efforts will be made to strengthen satellite-ground communication integration applications, lay out low-altitude network infrastructure construction, and promote deep coverage of 5G networks at sea.
At the same time, efforts are being made to promote the deep coverage of 5G networks at sea, build an ecosystem for innovative industrial development, and support the organization of top-tier events and activities.
(China News Finance)
New variables have emerged in China’s e-commerce industry; how can content become the key to successful product sales?
– China News Service
China News Service, February 11th: Title: “New Variables” Emerge in China’s E-commerce Industry – How Can Content Become the Key to Successful Product Sales?
Xia Bin, a reporter from China Finance News
“We came into e-commerce late, but we realized from the start that content was important if you wanted to stand out from the millions of stores.
Fangfang, an 90s girl from Guangdong who runs a health food store on Douyin e-commerce, has made her offline business that has been around for over three decades blossom online.
Imitating the style of old Hong Kong films and pairing them with classic Cantonese songs, the @FangFangYirenShi Douyin account offers beautifully crafted videos that are truly refreshing.
At the recently held Douyin e-commerce event “Searching for Peers: A Special Session on Sharing High-Quality Content,” Fangfang, as a representative of high-quality creators, spoke about her daily creative experiences and insights.
She said at the event: “The carefully produced video has attracted a lot of attention from netizens. Many people are interested in the ingredients from my home and want to try making delicious meals together with me, which has suddenly opened up new sales opportunities for us.”
‘
Fangfang helped more people fall in love with the “taste of Guangdong” through her videos on making soups. During one live broadcast, she sold up to 300,000 servings of nourishing ingredients, saving an old family business that was on the verge of closing.
“No content, no e-commerce.” As short videos and live-streaming e-commerce continue to develop, people’s expectations and standards for e-commerce content are entering a new phase.
In the early stages of the development of live-streaming sales, live streaming rooms often attracted users with low-price discounts, and the price advantage seemed to be the only selling point at that time.
In recent years, there have been both phenomenon-level influencers such as Liu Guohong and Dongfang Zhenxuan, as well as many experts and businesses that are less well-known to the general public but have emerged in niche vertical fields. These individuals and businesses have improved their long-term operational efficiency by consistently producing high-quality content that aligns with the tone of their respective brands.
Gao Yaxuan from Douyin E-commerce Content Creator Operations said that in the past year, 6.27 million creators have monetized their content through Douyin E-commerce, with their creation volume increasing by over 250% and total transaction value rising more than twice.
“Behind these numbers, we can sense an author community that is thriving and full of vitality.”
Gao Yaxuan said.
The Communication Innovation and Future Media Experimental Platform at Beijing Normal University previously released the “E-commerce Industry Content Ecology Health Index (ECHI) Report,” which analyzes the importance of high-quality content as a “new variable” in the current e-commerce sector from a data-driven perspective. The report uses this index to assess the content ecology of 27 major domestic e-commerce platforms.
According to the report on e-commerce industry content ecosystem health index rankings, Douyin E-commerce, Kuaishou, Tmall, Pinduoduo, and JD rank among the top five.
The report argues that the content ecosystem in the e-commerce industry is a comprehensive concept that integrates e-commerce with various types of content. However, not all types of content are suitable for integration with e-commerce. High-quality PGC (professionally produced content) and UGC (user-generated content) are the ideal mediums for this integration. The greater the value of the content platform, the more diverse the scenarios for consumption and promotion become, and the higher the potential for integrating e-commerce elements into these platforms. Consequently, the commercial value increases, leading to a higher proportion of e-commerce-related content production and consumption that spans both public and private domains.
At the event, Professor Hu Guoming, of the Beijing Teachers University School of Journalism and Communication, and Chairman of the China Media Economics and Management Professional Committee, gave an analytical explanation of the report.
He said that in terms of content value, the current e-commerce industry has transitioned from “accessibility to consumption” to “quality-oriented consumption,” and high-quality, professional, and differentiated content is the “hard currency” of the e-commerce industry.
At the same time, content has become the foundation and key driver for the new stage of e-commerce development. Services such as knowledge-based payments, specialized knowledge, and PGC (Professional Generated Content) provided by KOLs (Key Opinion Leaders) have begun to become standard features in e-commerce live broadcasts.
Looking ahead to the future development of the e-commerce industry, Yu Guoming puts forward two suggestions.
One approach is to enhance the overall health and quality of the e-commerce content ecosystem from the perspective of its structural organization. This involves establishing positive standards for content creation and management, thereby achieving a balanced and dynamic system index that reflects the health of the e-commerce industry's content ecosystem.
Another aspect is to consider the external ecosystem: it is necessary to achieve healthy development in the content e-commerce industry, as well as value synergy and co-creation with the surrounding environment.
“The future of the e-commerce industry will require more support in terms of data and artificial intelligence to predict the stability of its development. In addition, it is necessary to provide merchants with a more standardized and healthy environment for growth, enabling the coordination of values among companies, users, products, and services within the e-commerce sector, and thus jointly creating a healthy content ecosystem.”
“(End)”
(VOA Chinese) – On Friday (February 10), the Biden administration blacklisted six Chinese entities suspected of involvement in the spy balloon program.
The US Department of Commerce stated that the five Chinese companies and one research institute were helping to modernize the Chinese military, particularly in aerospace projects, including airships and aircraft.
Blacklisted companies have difficulty accessing US technology exports.
The list is called an “entity list,” and companies that enter it will be unable to purchase technology or goods from US suppliers unless they obtain a special export license from the US Department of Commerce.
The companies that have been added to the blacklist are: Beijing Nanjiang Aerospace Technology Co., Ltd., the 48th Research Institute of China Electronics Technology Group, Dongguan Lingkong Remote Sensing Technology Co., Ltd., Yingmen Aviation Technology Group Co., Ltd., Guangzhou Tianhaixiang Aviation Technology Co., Ltd., and Shanxi Yingmen Aviation Technology Group Co., Ltd.
Prior to this, the White House had indicated that it was considering broader measures to “expose and address” China’s larger-scale surveillance activities that threatened US national security.
The balloon incident has sparked further tensions between China and the US, with US Secretary of State Hillary Clinton cancelling a visit to China.
On February 4, the US shot down an air balloon, and China raised a serious protest to the US embassy in Beijing over America’s severe interference and damage to both sides’ efforts and progress toward stabilizing Sino-US relations.
Based on the existing evidence of debris and information from China’s military procurement platforms, the U.S. government has concluded that the manufacturer of the balloon “has a direct connection with the Chinese People’s Liberation Army” and is a supplier approved by the Chinese military.
Mao Ning, a spokesperson for the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs, stated at a press conference on Friday that regarding the incident where a Chinese non-military airship accidentally entered U.S. airspace due to force majeure, China has already explained the situation and clarified its position on multiple occasions.
According to the website of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, she added that the relevant resolutions passed by the U.S. Congress are purely political manipulations and sensationalism.
China is strongly dissatisfied with this and firmly opposes it.
Matthew Axelrod, the US Department of Commerce’s Assistant Secretary for Export Enforcement, said: “Today’s action demonstrates our joint efforts to identify and stop China from using spy balloons that violate the airspace of the United States and more than 40 countries.
‘
Reuters reports that an employee of Tianhai Xiang Aviation Technology Co., Ltd. in Guangzhou said he was unaware of sanctions and declined to comment further.
The Chinese Embassy in the United States has not yet commented on this information.
(Reuters et al.)
